<title>RUSSIA: Moscow launches municipal bond programme.</title>
<headline>Moscow launches municipal bond programme.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The City of Moscow launched its municipal bond programme on Wednesday, in a first auction of 10 billion roubles of six-month paper.</p>
<p>The sale was heavily oversubscribed, and the municipal bonds yielded an average 30.69 percent, in line with yields on Russian government paper.</p>
<p>Moscow joins a handful of Russian regions and cities, including St Petersburg and Tatarstan, which issue bonds regularly.</p>
<p>The City of Moscow plans to issue a total of 200 billion roubles of bonds in the first stage of its borrowing programme.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction:</p>
<p>    Series number		 MF73-3-00155</p>
<p>    Issue volume		  10 bln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		 1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		15.8 bln</p>
<p>    Sold			    8.59 bln</p>
<p>    Average price		 86.73 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price     85.32 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		 30.69 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			   182 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		 August 20, 1997</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
